  ;; ============================================================
  ;; PIN ASSIGNMENTS (documented as text annotation)
  ;; ============================================================
  (text "STM32H743VITx PIN ASSIGNMENT (Rev 2.0 - mapped to LQFP-100 pin numbers)\n\nPort names below were transcribed from the previous revision's notes and then\nconverted to package pin numbers using the KiCad MCU_ST_STM32H7 symbol, which is\ngenerated from the ST datasheet. Verified against the pins whose position is fixed:\nNRST=14, BOOT0=94, VBAT=6, VDDA=21, VREF+=20, VSSA=19, VCAP=48/73,\nVDD=11/27/50/75/100, VSS=10/26/49/74/99.\n\nTHREE CHANGES were forced when the old notes were converted:\n  UART4_TX  PA0 -> PB9  : PA0 is an ADC1 channel; the four analog inputs must stay\n                          on PA0-PA3, and PB9 was the only free UART4_TX pin.\n  UART4_RX  PC11 -> PB8 : PC11 is SDMMC1_D3. All five UART4_RX-capable pins were\n                          taken, so WDT_KICK vacated PB8.\n  WDT_KICK  PB8 -> PD9  : displaced by UART4_RX; it is a plain GPIO output.\n  LORA_RST / GSM_PWR_KEY moved off PC2/PC3: on the 100-pin package those are the\n                          dual-pad PC2_C/PC3_C analog variants, so plain GPIOs\n                          PB10/PB11 are used instead.\n  SD_CD was never assigned in the old notes; it is on PD15.\n\nSIGNAL         PORT   PIN\nADC1_CH0       PA0    pin 22\nADC1_CH1       PA1    pin 23\nADC1_CH2       PA2    pin 24\nADC1_CH3       PA3    pin 25\nBLE_RST        PD12   pin 59\nBLE_STATUS     PD13   pin 60\nDI_0           PD3    pin 84\nDI_1           PD7    pin 88\nDI_2           PE0    pin 97\nDI_3           PE1    pin 98\nDI_4           PE9    pin 39\nDI_5           PE10   pin 40\nDI_6           PE11   pin 41\nDI_7           PE12   pin 42\nDO_0           PE13   pin 43\nDO_1           PE14   pin 44\nDO_2           PE15   pin 45\nDO_3           PD14   pin 61\nETH_INT        PB0    pin 34\nETH_RST        PE3    pin 2\nFDCAN1_RX      PD0    pin 81\nFDCAN1_TX      PD1    pin 82\nGSM_PWR_KEY    PB11   pin 47\nGSM_STATUS     PD11   pin 58\nHSE_IN         PH0    pin 12\nHSE_OUT        PH1    pin 13\nI2C1_SCL       PB6    pin 92\nI2C1_SDA       PB7    pin 93\nLORA_DIO0      PC13   pin 7\nLORA_RST       PB10   pin 46\nLSE_IN         PC14   pin 8\nLSE_OUT        PC15   pin 9\nNSS_ETH        PE4    pin 3\nNSS_FLASH      PA15   pin 77\nNSS_LORA       PA4    pin 28\nNSS_WIFI       PB12   pin 51\nRS485_DE       PD4    pin 85\nSDMMC1_CLK     PC12   pin 80\nSDMMC1_CMD     PD2    pin 83\nSDMMC1_D0      PC8    pin 65\nSDMMC1_D1      PC9    pin 66\nSDMMC1_D2      PC10   pin 78\nSDMMC1_D3      PC11   pin 79\nSD_CD          PD15   pin 62\nSPI1_MISO      PA6    pin 30\nSPI1_MOSI      PB5    pin 91\nSPI1_SCK       PA5    pin 29\nSPI2_MISO      PB14   pin 53\nSPI2_MOSI      PB15   pin 54\nSPI2_SCK       PB13   pin 52\nSPI3_MISO      PB4    pin 90\nSPI3_MOSI      PB2    pin 36\nSPI3_SCK       PB3    pin 89\nSPI4_MISO      PE5    pin 4\nSPI4_MOSI      PE6    pin 5\nSPI4_SCK       PE2    pin 1\nSWCLK          PA14   pin 76\nSWDIO          PA13   pin 72\nUART4_RX       PB8    pin 95\nUART4_TX       PB9    pin 96\nUART7_RX       PE7    pin 37\nUART7_TX       PE8    pin 38\nUSART1_RX      PA10   pin 69\nUSART1_TX      PA9    pin 68\nUSART2_RX      PD6    pin 87\nUSART2_TX      PD5    pin 86\nUSB_DM         PA11   pin 70\nUSB_DP         PA12   pin 71\nWDT_KICK       PD9    pin 56\nWIFI_EN        PB1    pin 35\nWIFI_IRQ       PD10   pin 57\nWIFI_RST       PC0    pin 15\n\nSPARE GPIO: PC1(16) PC2_C(17) PC3_C(18) PA7(31) PC4(32) PC5(33) PD8(55) PC6(63)\n            PC7(64) PA8(67)\n\nJ10: 10-pin ARM SWD header. J11: USB-C (USB_OTG_FS, DFU). J12: UART debug console,\nwired to the buffered side of R14/R15. J13: BOOT0 jumper. J14: Tag-Connect TC2050."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "MCU-TEXT-0001")
  )
